BandIt v2 model code (vendored)

Source:  https://github.com/kwatcharasupat/bandit-v2
Commit:  d5563d9031e95fdaa3e5a73d5020b9a0df61adb6 (2025-07-29)
Paper:   K. N. Watcharasupat, C.-W. Wu, I. Orife, "Remastering Divide and
         Remaster: A Cinematic Audio Source Separation Dataset with
         Multilingual Support", arXiv:2407.07275.
License: Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory).

Files taken from upstream `src/models/bandit/` and `src/models/base.py`.
`film.py` is not vendored (unused by the Bandit model).

Modifications made for frootio (each modified file carries a header):
- Imports made package-relative (`frootio.stems.bandit`).
- base.py: `BaseEndToEndModule` derives from `torch.nn.Module` instead of
  `pytorch_lightning.LightningModule` (no Lightning dependency).
- utils.py: librosa `hz_to_midi`/`midi_to_hz` replaced by the identical
  numpy formulas; band-split classes not used by the Bandit model
  (vocal/bass/drum/mel specs, commented-out bark/ERB code, `__main__`) removed.
- bandsplit.py, maskestim.py, tfmodel.py: training-only activation
  checkpointing (`checkpoint_sequential`) and `torch.compile(..., disable=True)`
  wrappers removed; the wrapped modules are called directly. Unused
  `MaskEstimationModule` removed.

Model weights (not included here; downloaded at runtime from
https://zenodo.org/records/12701995) are licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 by their authors.
